{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Ger vetoshav anochi imakhem, ger</b> — that I came from a foreign land; <b>vetoshav</b> — that it is my intention to settle among you. Here Rashi explained: and if not, I will take it by law. And if you ask: but in the section of Lekh Lekha, regarding 'and the Canaanite and the Perizzite were then dwelling in the land,' Rashi explained that Abraham still had no portion in the land, for Abraham still had no offspring, and it is written 'to your seed I will give this land'; but now, in the section of Ḥayei Sarah, Isaac has been born, and he had a portion in the land." "<b>Give me a burial holding.</b> If I bury my dead in one of the fields of the city's men, today or tomorrow the owner of the field may come to plow, dig into the grave, and cast out the bones; but once you give me a burial holding, there is no concern that they would plow in it."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:05:24.088472370Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}